Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.15,0:00:02.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Kikkun!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.23,0:00:06.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnFredoka\b1\fs25\1c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\bord1.5\pos(118.4,60.8)}Bread Crusts, datsun!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.99,0:00:06.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm so glad we got so many bread crusts, tsun.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.39,0:00:08.13,Default,,0,0,0,,We were in front of the store for 5 hours,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.39,0:00:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,so persistence pays off.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.47,0:00:11.65,Default,,0,0,0,,You shouldn't give up on anything, tsun, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.91,0:00:12.71,Default,,0,0,0,,By the way,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.87,0:00:15.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I wonder why the edges of sliced bread are called "ears" ({\i1}*mimi*{\i0}).
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.87,0:00:15.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(188,21.333)}Mimi(耳) = ears
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.60,0:00:19.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, people have called the rims of things "ears" since long ago, tsun.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.86,0:00:23.53,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why the rims of sliced bread came to be called ears too, tsun.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.86,0:00:24.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Ehhh....
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.60,0:00:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,As expected of Tsuntsun.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.68,0:00:26.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You're my pride and joy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.32,0:00:28.71,Default,,0,0,0,,But you know, Daddy thinks...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.28,0:00:32.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Isn't it too sad for them to just be ears in name only?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.08,0:00:35.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to attach real ears to the sliced bread.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.84,0:00:38.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this just the hubris of someone with power?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.10,0:00:38.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(239.2,155.733)}Kikkun
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.10,0:00:38.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(287.2,250.667)}Milk bread
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.10,0:00:38.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(340,281.6)}Food chain
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.84,0:00:39.96,Default,,0,0,0,,No way, tsun.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.12,0:00:41.70,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just Daddy's kindness, tsun.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.96,0:00:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsuntsun...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.36,0:00:45.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll make some ears specifically for sliced bread, tsun.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.29,0:00:50.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, you told me to bring out some sliced bread, \Nso I did, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.09,0:00:53.39,Default,,0,0,0,,what on earth did you attach to my sliced bread?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.65,0:00:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Ears.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.37,0:00:55.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I can see they're ears just by looking!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.57,0:00:59.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm asking why you attached ears \Nto sliced bread in the first place!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.70,0:01:01.19,Default,,0,0,0,,It's out of Daddy's kindness, tsun-yo.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.49,0:01:03.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no idea what you're talking about.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.53,0:01:06.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Now the sliced bread can listen to \Nits heart's content, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.62,0:01:09.31,Default,,0,0,0,,More importantly, \Nwe can actually eat this, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.05,0:01:12.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Mogura, \Nthe sliced bread is listening, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.57,0:01:14.55,Default,,0,0,0,,It can hear you, that's so harsh, tsun.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.53,0:01:16.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, we'll be going then.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.93,0:01:19.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, take this creepy thing back home with you!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.53,0:01:20.39,Default,,0,0,0,,It's listening, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.61,0:01:21.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Good grief.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.09,0:01:23.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess I'll eat it tomorrow morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.56,0:01:26.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, you were listening, weren't you?
